g, being a local specialty. In an adjacent city called Jinju, crunchier Jinju-kkulppang is sold as a local specialty. Shortly after the Korean War, many bakeries in Tongyeong were sold. Fishermen and shipbuilding workers who worked on the beach simply ate a meal or snack because they could be kept for a long time despite the warm climate of Tongyeong."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kkulppang"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kkulppang"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["South Korean cuisine","cuisine/south-korean-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Red bean paste","ingredient/red-bean-paste"],["Syrup","ingredient/syrup"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Korean Bapsang","ref":"site/koreanbapsang-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"koreanbapsang.com","note":"Home-style Korean recipes from Hyosun, a Korean-American mom.","url":"https://www.koreanbapsang.com/category/recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from South Korean cuisine","links":[["Chalbori-ppang","dish/chalbori-ppang"],["Chimaek","dish/chimaek"],["Croffle","dish/croffle"],["Dak-galbi","dish/dak-galbi"],["Gilgeori toast","dish/gilgeori-toast"],["Hodu-gwaja","dish/hodu-gwaja"],["Hwangnam-ppang","dish/hwangnam-ppang"],["Jinju bibimbap","dish/jinju-bibimbap"],["Jjolmyeon","dish/jjolmyeon"],["Milmyeon","dish/milmyeon"],["Rabokki","dish/rabokki"],["So-tteok-so-tteok","dish/so-tteok-so-tteok"],["Tornado potato","dish/tornado-potato"],["Ttongppang","dish/ttongppang"],["Yangnyeom chicken","dish/yangnyeom-chicken"]]}]},"ingredient/peppermint":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/peppermint","n":"Peppermint","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Peppermint (Mentha × piperita) is a hybrid species of mint, a cross between watermint and spearmint. Indigenous to Europe and the Middle East, the plant is now widely spread and cultivated in many regions of the world. It is occasionally found in the wild with its parent species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-peppermint"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peppermint"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Peppermint bark","dish/peppermint-bark"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Candy cane","ingredient/candy-cane"],["Caramel","ingredient/caramel"],["Dark chocolate","ingredient/dark-chocolate"],["White chocolate","ingredient/white-chocolate"]]}]},"dish/pork-tenderloin-sandwich":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pork-tenderloin-sandwich","n":"Pork tenderloin sandwich","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Midwestern American cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["The pork tenderloin sandwich, also known as a breaded pork tenderloin sandwich (BPT), contains a breaded and fried cutlet similar to Wiener schnitzel and is popular in the Midwest region of the United States, especially in the states of Indiana, Illinois, Nebraska, Missouri, and Iowa. The sandwich is claimed to have originated at Nick's Kitchen restaurant in Huntington, Indiana, near Fort Wayne."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pork-tenderloin-sandwich"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pork_tenderloin_sandwich"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Midwestern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-midwestern-united-states"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Breaded cutlet","ingredient/breaded-cutlet"]]},{"h":"More from Midwestern American cuisine","links":[["Chicago-style relish","dish/chicago-style-relish"]]}]},"dish/quesadilla":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/quesadilla","n":"Quesadilla","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Mexican cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A quesadilla is a Mexican dish made from a tortilla folded in half or two tortillas that are 