h/wash-s-restaurant","n":"Wash's Restaurant","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Soul food","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Wash's Restaurant, later called Wash & Sons' Seafood Restaurant, Wash's Inn, and Wash's Catering, was an African-American family-owned and operated soul food restaurant that was in business for over 70 years, first in Atlantic City and then in Pleasantville, New Jersey. Established by Clifton and Alma Washington at 35 N. Kentucky Avenue, Atlantic City, in 1937, the original 20-seat location attained celebrity status for hosting the performers and patrons of the nightclubs in the Kentucky Avenue black entertainment district. The restaurant was known for its sausage sandwiches and soul food, and also served breakfast to customers leaving the 6 a.m. show at Club Harlem."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-wash-s-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wash's_Restaurant"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Soul food","cuisine/soul-food"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"The Soul Food Pot","ref":"site/thesoulfoodpot-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"thesoulfoodpot.com","note":"Shaunda Necole's blog of soul food and Southern recipes.","url":"https://thesoulfoodpot.com/recipe-index","suggested":true},{"name":"Cooks with Soul","ref":"site/cookswithsoul-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"cookswithsoul.com","note":"Soul food recipe site that also covers cookbooks by Black authors.","url":"https://cookswithsoul.com/2024-holiday-gift-guide-soul-food-cookbooks-by-black-authors/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Soul food","links":[["Buffalo ribs","dish/buffalo-ribs"],["Chitlins","dish/chitlins"],["Delta Cafe","dish/delta-cafe"],["Fair Deal Cafe","dish/fair-deal-cafe"],["Fried okra","dish/fried-okra"],["Red beans and rice","dish/red-beans-and-rice"],["Souley Vegan","dish/souley-vegan"],["Sylvia's Restaurant of Harlem","dish/sylvia-s-restaurant-of-harlem